    "created_at": "2024-07-02T11:41:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-07-02T11:41:42Z",
    "body": "If i read https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dialog-focusing-steps correctly, then the dialog itself should receive focus in step 4.\r\n\r\nA few lines down though it says this: \"If control is not [focusable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#focusable), this will do nothing. This would only happen if subject had no focus delegate, **and the user agent decided that [dialog](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-dialog-element) elements were not generally focusable**. In that case, any [earlier modifications](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#note-dialog-plus-focus-fixup) to the [focused area of the document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#focused-area-of-the-document) will apply.\"\r\n\r\nDoes that mean that the Safari behavior is correct as well?",
